---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Local Info
description: Repeaters, nets, clubs and meeting places for ham radio around Middletown, Ohio.
---
<section class="wrap page-head">
  <h1>Local Info</h1>
  <p class="lead">Where to listen, where to talk, and where to meet other hams around {{ site.communities | join(", ") }}.</p>
  <p class="muted">Details change. Entries show when I last confirmed them, and anything marked <span class="mono">[TODO]</span> is still unverified. Check with the club or net before you rely on a frequency or time.</p>
  <ul class="jump" aria-label="On this page">
    <li><a href="#repeaters">Repeaters</a></li>
    <li><a href="#nets">Nets</a></li>
    <li><a href="#clubs">Clubs &amp; meeting places</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="repeaters" aria-labelledby="rep-h">
  <h2 id="rep-h">Repeaters</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>repeater</strong> is a radio station, usually on a tall building or tower, that
    receives your signal and rebroadcasts it, so a small handheld radio can reach across town.
    To use one you tune to its <strong>output</strong> frequency (what you hear), transmit on a
    slightly different frequency set by its <strong>offset</strong>, and sometimes send a quiet
    <strong>PL tone</strong> (a sub-audible signal that opens the repeater). Frequencies are in
    megahertz (MHz).
  </p>
  <ul class="cards">
    {%- for r in repeaters %}
    <li class="card">
      <h3>{{ r.name }}{% if r.sample %} <span class="tag tag--sample">Sample</span>{% endif %}</h3>
      <dl class="specs">
        <div><dt>Output</dt><dd class="mono">{{ r.output }}</dd></div>
        {%- if r.offset %}<div><dt>Offset</dt><dd class="mono">{{ r.offset }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if r.tone %}<div><dt>Tone</dt><dd class="mono">{{ r.tone }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if r.mode %}<div><dt>Mode</dt><dd>{{ r.mode }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if r.location %}<div><dt>Location</dt><dd>{{ r.location }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if r.coverage %}<div><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>{{ r.coverage }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if r.sponsor %}<div><dt>Sponsor</dt><dd>{{ r.sponsor }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if r.status %}<div><dt>Status</dt><dd>{{ r.status }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
      </dl>
      {%- if r.notes %}<p class="card__note">{{ r.notes }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if r.verified %}<p class="card__verified muted">Last confirmed <span class="mono">{{ r.verified }}</span></p>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="nets" aria-labelledby="net-h">
  <h2 id="net-h">Nets</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>net</strong> is a scheduled on-air meetup: a host called <em>net control</em> runs
    the session while hams <strong>check in</strong> by announcing their callsign. Some nets are
    social, some teach procedures, and some practice emergency communications. Newcomers are
    usually welcome to just listen the first time.
  </p>
  <ul class="cards">
    {%- for n in nets %}
    <li class="card">
      <h3>{{ n.name }}{% if n.sample %} <span class="tag tag--sample">Sample</span>{% endif %}</h3>
      {%- if n.kind %}<p class="event__tags"><span class="tag">{{ n.kind | replace("-", " ") | capitalize }}</span></p>{% endif %}
      <dl class="specs">
        <div><dt>When</dt><dd>{{ n.schedule }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Where</dt><dd class="mono">{{ n.where }}</dd></div>
        {%- if n.mode %}<div><dt>Mode</dt><dd>{{ n.mode }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if n.contact %}<div><dt>Contact</dt><dd>{{ n.contact }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
      </dl>
      {%- if n.description %}<p>{{ n.description }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if n.link %}<p><a href="{{ n.link }}" rel="noopener">More about {{ n.name }}</a></p>{% endif %}
      {%- if n.verified %}<p class="card__verified muted">Last confirmed <span class="mono">{{ n.verified }}</span></p>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="clubs" aria-labelledby="club-h">
  <h2 id="club-h">Clubs &amp; meeting places</h2>
  <p>
    Clubs are the fastest way to learn the hobby: you meet people who will happily answer
    questions, help with your first antenna, and sometimes run license classes and exam sessions.
    Most meet in public places like libraries, community centers, or restaurants.
  </p>
  <ul class="cards">
    {%- for c in clubs %}
    <li class="card">
      <h3>{{ c.name }}{% if c.sample %} <span class="tag tag--sample">Sample</span>{% endif %}</h3>
      <p class="event__tags"><span class="tag">{{ (c.kind or "club") | capitalize }}</span></p>
      <dl class="specs">
        {%- if c.schedule %}<div><dt>When</dt><dd>{{ c.schedule }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if c.meeting_place %}<div><dt>Where</dt><dd>{{ c.meeting_place }}{% if c.address %}<br>{{ c.address }}{% endif %}</dd></div>{% endif %}
        {%- if c.contact %}<div><dt>Contact</dt><dd>{{ c.contact }}</dd></div>{% endif %}
      </dl>
      {%- if c.description %}<p>{{ c.description }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if c.website %}<p><a href="{{ c.website }}" rel="noopener">Website<span class="visually-hidden"> for {{ c.name }}</span></a></p>{% endif %}
      {%- if c.verified %}<p class="card__verified muted">Last confirmed <span class="mono">{{ c.verified }}</span></p>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap section teaser">
  <h2>See something wrong, or know a group I missed?</h2>
  <p>Ham information goes stale quickly. If you run a net, repeater, or club in the area, I'd love to hear about it.</p>
  <p><a class="button" href="{{ site.contact.url }}">{{ site.contact.label }}</a></p>
</section>
